version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-loops
description: >-
  The loop file format shared by the kernel and tools: the schema (schema.ts)
  and the compiled form (compiled.ts).
context:
  - >-
    The kernel side of loops is src/kernel/loops/.
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  loop-schema:
    description: >-
      #loop-schema (docs/specs/gnomon-loops.md §2, §3.1, §3.4, §3.5; build
      plan LP1) in src/loops/schema.ts, exported as @a-company/gnomon/loops.
      The loop:v2 definition: types, validateLoop (precise {path, code,
      message} issues) and compileLoop to the canonical JSON the kernel reads
      (.paradigm/loops/<id>.loop.json; the kernel never parses YAML, zero
      runtime deps). Rules: closed shape; kebab ids <= 64; every edge target a
      node or terminal (@goal/@stop/@pause); goal names a check node, a run
      goal declares goal.inputs, only check/call nodes reach @goal (LL2);
      argv literal (no {{), argv0 never in the kernel INTERPRETER_DENYLIST
      (imported from #prefix-policy) or python*, never .cmd/.bat; judge and
      summarize nodes have no tools; continuous needs cooldown >= 60 s
      (MIN_AUTOMATION_PERIOD_MS), a goal or run.rounds, and day.runs or
      day.computeSec; call is id@hash8, cycles and depth > 3 refused given
      the known loops. 8.0 subset: model.use claude|any, escalate other than
      never, the claude opt-in block, cron, sentinel.incident.opened, bash
      tools and envelope fields are refused LANDS_IN_8_1 ("lands in 8.1").
      Compile fills every default (absent budget field = global default,
      never unbounded), durations in seconds, edges expanded per verdict,
      flows resolved to path globs from a flow index (else symbolic with a
      FLOWS_UNRESOLVED warning); canonicalLoopJson is the sorted-key hashing
      form, loopFileJson the indented file form. Aegis LP1 review: @goal only
      from goal.node or a call, and any @goal edge needs a goal block; a call
      pin must equal loopContentHash(callee) (sha256 of canonicalJson of the
      parsed definition, never file bytes) and a call reaching @goal needs a
      callee goal; argv0 never a BUILD_TOOLS entry except tsc/vitest/jest
      (LOOP_ARGV0_CHECKER_ALLOW); programName strips trailing dots/spaces,
      .exe and .com; land paths never under node_modules; NaN/Infinity
      refused; compiled `protected` = node_modules + goal.inputs + repo
      argv words across the call chain; `argv0Interpreter` recorded via
      readShebang. The shared INTERPRETER_DENYLIST gained cmd, powershell,
      pwsh, wscript, cscript, mshta, arch, script, stdbuf, setsid, chroot,
      sandbox-exec and busybox; loop-choice joined NEVER_STANDING_KINDS.
      LP2: compiled.sourceHash = loopContentHash(the parsed YAML), the hash a
      caller's pin names; src/loops/compiled.ts validateCompiledLoop is the
      kernel's re-validation of a .loop.json (decompile, validateLoop, compile
      again with the file's own budgets/flowPaths/interpreters, byte compare;
      protected and callsResolved are the kernel's own).
      TD-2026-10-23-268/448: `env: [NAME, ...]` on check and act nodes (<= 32
      names matching ^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$, no duplicates, never a hazard per
      runner/env.ts loopEnvHazard: ENV_REFUSED; judge/summarize:
      ENV_NOT_ALLOWED); loop-level `envFiles` (<= 8; repo-relative without ..,
      ~/ or absolute; BAD_ENV_FILE, ENV_FILE_DUPLICATE, ENV_FILES_TOO_MANY),
      `redact: on|off` and `network: on|off` (YAML 1.1 booleans accepted). All
      compile only when used, so existing loops hash as before;
      validateCompiledLoop keeps them.
    path: src/loops/schema.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, loops, paradigm-8, security]
    tests:
      - test/loop-compiled.test.ts
      - test/loop-schema.test.ts
